{# The Payment Status row of a sell-side document's Info card.

   Small, and the highest-correctness thing on this screen to have exactly one copy of: it is the
   one field where the badge's COLOUR is the answer. Paid is a green `badge success`; everything
   else — Unpaid, Partially Paid, Overdue, and any status added later — is the same red
   `badge danger-soft`, which is what both screens already did and what makes an unpaid document
   findable by eye down a page of grey fields.

   Two callers. The ORDER's value is rolled up from its invoices (OrderPaymentRollup): since #539
   stage 4 the order carries no payment status of its own, because money is the invoice's
   question. The INVOICE's is derived from its own payment rows. Two different derivations of one
   vocabulary, which is why the value is passed in and never reached for here.

   The quote has no such row and never will: nothing is owed on a document nobody has accepted.

   Deliberately NOT the document-status badge beside it. That one is `js-order-status-badge` on
   the order — the hook the status modal writes the new value into — and `badge order-status
   order-status-<key>` on the invoice and the quote, and it is out of scope pending the wider
   status overhaul.

   Parameters
   ----------
   value  required  the payment status as a plain string — PaymentStatus::value, never the enum,
                    so the two callers hand over the same kind of thing. #}
<div class="detail-row">
    <label>Payment Status:</label>
    {% if value == 'Paid' %}
        <span class="badge success">Paid</span>
    {% else %}
        <span class="badge danger-soft" style="color:#e11d48; background:#fff1f2;">{{ value }}</span>
    {% endif %}
</div>
